6. Increment and decrement operators
- ++ increases a value by one.
- -- decreases a value by one.
int x = 5;

x++;
printf("%d\n", x);  // 6

x--;
printf("%d\n", x);  // 5

A useful distinction:
- y = x++ assigns the old value of x to y, then increments x.
- y = ++x increments x first, then assigns the new value to y.

